    "['no synchronization', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize', 'parent_command': ['set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco \"no synchronization\" BGP command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize\\n##\\n\\nNote:\\n1. In Juniper, this is configured under the specific BGP group where synchronization needs to be disabled.\\n2. You would need to replace `<group-name>` with the actual BGP group name from your Juniper configuration.\\n3. Like Cisco, Juniper defaults to no synchronization in BGP, but this command explicitly disables it if needed.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize'}]]": 1,
